{{#hasRedundantReads}}
## Redundant file reads

Files read more than once in the same session. Re-reading after an `Edit` is usually wasted — `Edit` already errors loudly on failure, so the harness state is trustworthy.

| Session | File | Reads | Span (min) | Max gap (min) | Pattern |
|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---|
{{#redundantReads}}
| `{{sessionId}}` | `{{filePath}}` | {{reads}} | {{spanMinutes}} | {{maxGapMinutes}} | {{pattern}} |
{{/redundantReads}}

`Pattern` distinguishes a tight **hunting loop** (≥ 3 reads, max gap ≤ 5 min — the agent is retrying) from a **spread across session** (max gap ≥ 30 min — incidental re-reads, often benign) and a **tight cluster** in between. Hunting loops are the high-priority targets; *spread across session* rows usually don't need an `AGENTS.md` rule.

{{/hasRedundantReads}}
{{#hasEditLoops}}
## Edit failure loops

Sessions where `Edit` failed two or more times against the same file — typically the agent hunting for the right `old_string` and retrying with tweaks.

