## Tool performance

| Tool | Calls | Avg ms | p95 ms | Avg result bytes |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
{{#performance}}
| `{{tool}}` | {{calls}} | {{avgMs}} | {{p95Ms}} | {{avgOut}} |
{{/performance}}

Latency tails (p95) tend to surface tools that occasionally do heavy work — long shell commands, slow MCP servers, large file reads. If a tool's p95 is much higher than its average, consider whether the agent could narrow its inputs (smaller globs, shorter shell pipelines, paged reads).

